our team recently received a screening  of the bumblebee movie and were happy to  say that the film takes a step in the  right direction to becoming the more  quintessential transformers story that  fans of the franchise will love opening  on the war for Cybertron  it's immediately apparent that the  previous aesthetic of the film has been  stripped away in favor of a more bright  and colorful tone gone on the darkly lit  bowels and hard to make out showdowns  replaced with eye-catching scenes and  neatly designed face offs those who  expect the CGI heavy affair know exactly  what they're in for  and bumblebee by far tops the series in  terms of special-effects cinematography  and character design this feels like the  80s cartoon brought to life in an  astounding way and is something fresh  and invigorating for the franchise  Charlie played by Hailee Steinfeld feels  like the perfect female counterpart to  Shia LaBeouf and she does well at  playing the enamoured eighties tomboy  that has been made famous by the likes  of stranger things et and it whilst  there are aspects that are slightly  derivative it's still engaging to see  this newest a and Hayley does a great  job she wonderfully restores the Beatle  car and it's refreshing to see the  Transformers take on something that  resembles a rust bucket rather than the  top-of-the-line sports model this herby  vibe definitely makes the characters  endearing early on and both adults and  children will find themselves  gravitating to the way that transformers  are reintroduced here Haley brings a lot  of fun to the film and I love seeing her  getting chased down by cop cars and she  genuinely seems like she's strapped in  for the ride and having fun with it John  Cena equally does a serviceable job as  an army soldier even though he doesn't  have as much screen time as you would  expect for the star this film isn't  going to blow you away plot wise and you  could probably guess the majority of the  movies moments from watching the trailer  alone however that doesn't mean that  this isn't an enjoyable journey for both  newcomers and hot core fans alike  overall this is a fun-filled kids movie  and there's a certain innocence to it  that was lacking in the original  Transformers films this writes a lot of  the wrongs from those movies in a  fantastic way and whilst is imperfect  it's very hard to ding the movie just  because  aspects are slightly predictable this  film is playing heavily on nostalgia so  if you like things like The Goonies ET  Honey I Shrunk the Kids and more you  will love it the movie restored a lot of  my faith in the franchise and really  feels like it's setting up some stellar  things to come down the line overall we  had fun with the movie and that's why it  scores a 7 out of 10 so are you excited  for the bumblebee movie and what you  hope to see in it comment below and let  me know and if you enjoyed this video  then make sure that you subscribe to the  channel and keep an eye out for my  everything explained video which will be  breaking down all of the major aspects  of the film this is a channel for people  who are mad into movies so if you want  to be kept up to date with all of the  latest news reviews previews breakdowns  and more hit subscribe thanks again for  taking the time to watch this I've been  definition you've been the best I'll see  you next time  take care peace  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

